USAGE: run_tofino_model.sh -p <p4_program_name> [OPTIONS -- TOFINO_MODEL_OPTIONS]
Options for running tofino-model:
  -c TARGET_CONFIG_FILE
    TARGET_CONFIG_FILE that describes P4 artifacts of the device
  -d NUM
    Instantiate NUM devices in tofino-model
  -k PKG_SIZE
    Number of Subdevices per Device (1-2) package size
  -f PORTINFO_FILE
    Read port to veth mapping information from PORTINFO_FILE
  -g
    Run with gdb
  -h
    Print this message
  -p
    Program name, a shortcut for specifying the path to the conf file with -c
  -q
    Quiet the model
  --conf-disable
    Set model to not use p4 target config file
  --int-port-loop <pipe-bitmap>
    Put ports in internal loopback mode for specified pipes (0xf for all pipes)
  --log-dir
    Specify log file directory
  --json-logs-enable
    Enable the JSON event log stream
  --pkt-log-len
    Specify packet log length in bytes
  --use-pcie-veth
    Set model to use veth for pcie packets
  --dod-test-mode
    Set model to send every 10th DeflectOnDrop packet to Port0
  --arch <tf1|tf2|tf2m|tf3>
    Specifiy the chip architecture, defaults to Tofino
  --no-port-monitor
    Do not monitor interfaces to detect port up/down events
  --time-disable
    Do not automatically increment time
